          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09",
          "portId": "root",
          "name": "Lionel Validation Study 09"
        },
        "title": "Lionel Validation Study 09",
        "purpose": "Test the existing grammar against a live episode that remains unusually focused and mostly linear.",
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.summary",
          "label": "Lionel Validation Study 09"
        },
        "payload": "node.web.summary",
        "intent": "node",
        "key": "node.web.summary",
        "viewRole": "summary",
        "viewKind": "display",
        "semanticLevel": "summary",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        },
        "markdown": "# Lionel Validation Study 09\n\n## Crisis Briefing Thesis Monologue\n\nA roughly **1:17:42** live episode arguing against an expanded U.S. war with Iran through three contemporary warning stories, Vietnam-era precedent, Iranian historical context, political realignment, audience polling, and personal memory.\n\n**Sequence controller:** `thesis`  \n**Navigation mode:** `mostly-linear`  \n**Container:** `live`  \n**Support structure:** `evidence-bundle`  \n**New episode family required:** no\n\n`RAISE STAKES -> SPONSOR -> BUNDLE WARNINGS -> DEFINE NATIONAL INTEREST -> PERSONALIZE COST -> HISTORICAL TEST -> MAP REALIGNMENT -> TAKE OPPONENT PERSPECTIVE -> POLL AUDIENCE -> RETURN TO THESIS -> PERSONAL MEMORY -> COMMUNITY CLOSE`\n\nA live Lionel episode does not have to be branch-and-return.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
