        "markdown": "# 📺 Source and Attribution Boundary\n\n**Duration represented:** approximately 1:17:42.\n\nLionel opens by asking whether Americans are willing to risk soldiers' lives in a war with Iran and immediately frames possible war and renewed draft machinery as vastly more consequential than the Tyler Robinson or Erica Kirk stories. \n\nThe transcript contains political arguments, historical claims, military assessments, allegations about motives, speculation about public officials, descriptions of possible retaliation, and live audience comments. Those remain attributed to Lionel or the quoted audience participant.\n\nThis graph studies composition and rhetoric, not the independent truth of those claims.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-central",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Central Observation",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -540,
