      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nStudy 09 is a useful corrective to Studies 06 and 08.\n\nIt is a **live Lionel monologue**, but it does not wander through a large persistent thread set. The episode remains overwhelmingly focused on one proposition:\n\n**Lionel argues that expanding a U.S. conflict with Iran would create greater danger to Americans than Iran itself presently poses.**\n\nHe develops that proposition cumulatively through contemporary warning stories, draft history, political realignment, Iranian historical grievances, audience questions, and personal Vietnam-era memory.\n\nSo `live` does **not** imply `branch-and-return`.\n\nContainer, sequence controller, and navigation mode are genuinely independent dimensions.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-seg1",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "1 · Existential Stakes Hook",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1580,
