        },
        "markdown": "# 5 · Draft History and Personal Cost\n## 27:18–31:06\n\nLionel turns to the Vietnam-era draft, recalls resistance, Canada, prison, campus unrest, and the political effect of middle-class families realizing their sons could be sent to fight. He then asks viewers to imagine the same cost falling on their own children or grandchildren. \n\n**Function:** translate abstract foreign policy into a household-level cost and use historical precedent to forecast political consequences.\n\n**Existing moves:** `Adds Historical Context`, `Personalizes Stakes`, `Identifies Pattern`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
