        "markdown": "# 6 · Anti-War Coalition Realignment\n## 31:06–40:34\n\nLionel says the Iran issue is splitting MAGA and Republicans between an `America First` anti-intervention position and figures he associates with an older interventionist worldview. He then notes that parts of the anti-war left now occupy the same side of this issue as paleoconservative and libertarian-leaning voices. \n\nHe crystallizes the argument as a reversal: Iran itself is not the existential danger in his model; **a war with Iran is**, because its costs would be paid through energy prices, infrastructure risk, conscription, and political cohesion. \n\n**Validation:** `Coalition Mapping` from Study 06 recurs in a tightly focused thesis episode.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
