        "markdown": "# 7 · Historical Perspective-Taking\n## 40:34–46:19\n\nLionel explicitly asks viewers to look at the relationship **from Iran's point of view** and walks through historical grievances he believes shape Iranian perceptions of the United States, including the 1953 coup, the Shah, the Iran-Iraq war, 1988 naval conflict and Iran Air Flight 655, the killing of Qasem Soleimani, and later Israeli and U.S. military operations. \n\n**Function:** model the adversary's historical memory without requiring sympathy with the adversary.\n\nThis strongly validates the Study 06 move previously described as `Strategic Empathy` or `Models an Opponent's Perspective`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-seg8",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "8 · Live Poll and Audience Sampling",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 2360,
