      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09"
        },
        "markdown": "# ⚙️ Important Disconfirmation\n## Live Is Not Branch-and-Return\n\nStudies 06 and 08 strongly established `branch-and-return` as a recurring Lionel live behavior.\n\nStudy 09 shows it is **not mandatory**.\n\nThis episode contains live chat and spontaneous remarks, but the central Iran-war argument remains continuously active. Audience interventions are mostly absorbed into the same topic rather than opening long-lived side threads.\n\nTherefore these dimensions should stay independent:\n\n- `containerMode = live`\n- `sequenceController = thesis`\n- `navigationMode = mostly-linear`\n\nThis is stronger evidence for the model than another branch-heavy stream would have been.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-chat",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Live Chat Has Multiple Structural Roles",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1220,
        "y": 540
      },
      "width": 680,
      "height": 590,
      "ports": [
        {
