          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09"
        },
        "markdown": "# 💬 Live Chat Has Multiple Structural Roles\n\nThe corpus now shows at least three uses of live audience input:\n\n1. **navigation trigger**\n   - a message opens a side branch\n\n2. **poll response**\n   - viewers answer a structured question such as `1` or `2`\n\n3. **hypothesis contribution**\n   - viewers propose explanations that Lionel evaluates in real time\n\nStudy 09 strongly demonstrates the second and third forms.  \n\nSo `Chat Message` should probably carry a role or relationship rather than being treated as one generic interruption:\n\n- `triggersBranch`\n- `answersPoll`\n- `proposesHypothesis`\n- `corrects`\n- `suppliesLead`\n- `buildsRapport`",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-perspective",
      "type": "markdown",
