      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔭 Perspective-Taking Recurs\n\nStudy 06 showed Lionel trying to understand an opponent's strategic objectives without endorsing them.\n\nStudy 09 repeats the operation at a larger scale by asking viewers to reconstruct the U.S.-Iran relationship from the Iranian historical viewpoint. \n\nThat supports a more general reusable move:\n\n## `Lionel Models Another Actor's Perspective`\n\nPossible fields:\n\n- actor\n- historical context\n- perceived grievance\n- inferred incentive\n- degree of endorsement\n- uncertainty\n\nThis is broader and cleaner than a topic-specific `Strategic Empathy` class.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786076913184,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study09-compare",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Comparison Across Nine Studies",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": 1230
      },
      "width": 800,
      "height": 760,
      "ports": [
