      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-validation-study-09"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📏 Confidence and Next Step\n\n## High confidence\n- Study 09 belongs to the thesis-monologue family\n- a live container does not determine navigation mode\n- evidence bundles are distinct from media queues\n- historical perspective-taking is a recurring Lionel operation\n- coalition mapping recurs outside Study 06\n- live chat has structural roles beyond branch triggering\n- the grammar continues to converge\n\n## Medium confidence\n- `Evidence Bundle` deserves an explicit shared node type rather than ordinary grouped references\n- `Personalizes Stakes` deserves a named Lionel move\n- audience polls deserve their own production node rather than a `Chat Prompt` role\n\n## Study implication\nThe next specimen should be treated almost entirely as a held-out test. At nine transcripts, genuinely new episode families should now require strong evidence rather than novelty of subject matter alone.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
